    overview: 'This six-day private safari brings together three of Tanzania’s defining wildlife landscapes. Start with a gentle arrival in Arusha, explore elephant country in Tarangire, spend two nights in the Serengeti and finish with a crater-floor game drive in Ngorongoro. Optional walking safaris, a hot-air balloon flight, a Maasai village visit and Olduvai Gorge can be added when they fit your dates and permits.',
    suitability: 'For first-time visitors who want the classic Northern Circuit in a focused private route, with the choice to add more time on foot or connect the wildlife to local culture.',
    facts: [['Trip style', 'Private Northern Circuit safari'], ['Starts / ends', 'Kilimanjaro Airport / Arusha'], ['Signature experiences', 'Serengeti nights and Ngorongoro Crater'], ['Optional add-ons', 'Walking, balloon and cultural visits']],
    days: [
      { label: 'Day 1', title: 'Arrive and settle into Arusha', location: 'Kilimanjaro International Airport → Arusha', stay: 'Under The Shade Safari Lodge, Arusha', meals: 'Lunch & dinner', note: 'Arrival transfer and safari briefing', copy: 'Arrive at Kilimanjaro International Airport, where your professional driver-guide welcomes you and transfers you to Arusha. Use the first afternoon to rest, meet the team and prepare for the days ahead before dinner and your overnight stay.' },
      { label: 'Day 2', title: 'Tarangire elephant country', location: 'Arusha → Tarangire National Park → Karatu', stay: 'Mvuli Lodge, Karatu', meals: 'Lunch & dinner', note: 'Guided walking safari is optional and must be pre-booked', copy: 'After breakfast, drive to Tarangire National Park for morning and afternoon game drives among ancient baobabs, elephant herds, lions, leopards, giraffes, buffalo and more than 550 bird species. Follow the Tarangire River, where wildlife gathers in the dry season, or add a permitted walking safari. Continue to Karatu in the late afternoon for dinner and your overnight stay.' },
      { label: 'Day 3', title: 'Into the Central Serengeti', location: 'Karatu → Central Serengeti National Park', stay: 'Golden Safari Camp or Moyo Tented Camp', meals: 'Breakfast, lunch & dinner', note: 'En-route game viewing begins after the park entry', copy: 'Travel through the Ngorongoro Highlands toward the legendary Serengeti, with time for photographs at crater-rim viewpoints. As the landscape opens into the plains, begin an en-route game drive with chances to see lions, cheetahs, elephants, giraffes, wildebeest and zebras before arriving at camp for dinner under the stars.' },
      { label: 'Day 4', title: 'A full day on the Serengeti plains', location: 'Central Serengeti National Park', stay: 'Golden Safari Camp or Moyo Tented Camp', meals: 'Breakfast, lunch & dinner', note: 'Balloon safari and Maasai village visit are optional and must be pre-booked', copy: 'Spend the day exploring the Serengeti on extended game drives shaped around current sightings and the best light. For a different perspective, add a sunrise hot-air balloon safari followed by a bush breakfast, or arrange a Maasai village visit to learn about local traditions before returning to camp.' },
      { label: 'Day 5', title: 'Serengeti to the Ngorongoro Highlands', location: 'Serengeti → Ngorongoro Conservation Area', stay: 'Mvuli Lodge, Ngorongoro Highlands', meals: 'Breakfast, lunch & dinner', note: 'Olduvai Gorge and crater-rim walking safari are optional', copy: 'Take a final morning game drive in the Serengeti, then travel toward the Ngorongoro Conservation Area. Add a visit to Olduvai Gorge Museum, known as the Cradle of Mankind, or join a ranger-guided walking safari along the crater rim for wide views across the caldera. Settle into your Karatu lodge by evening.' },
      { label: 'Day 6', title: 'Ngorongoro Crater and departure', location: 'Ngorongoro Crater → Arusha → Kilimanjaro International Airport', stay: 'No accommodation', meals: 'Breakfast & lunch', note: 'Departure timing is coordinated around your flight', copy: 'After an early breakfast, descend 600 metres into the Ngorongoro Crater for a final game drive. The crater is home to more than 30,000 animals and offers one of Tanzania’s strongest chances to see the Big Five, including black rhino. Enjoy a picnic lunch inside the crater, then drive back to Arusha and continue to the airport for your departure.' },
    ],
